        "nobel_worthiness": "The Aharonov–Bohm effect and Berry phase revealed that quantum phases have observable physical consequences and reshaped understanding across many areas of physics.",
        "attribution": "Aharonov is central to the first effect and Berry to the general geometric phase; both contributions are individually identifiable, though they are distinct discoveries.",
        "maturity": "The effects have been observed and used widely, and their conceptual significance has endured for decades.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Combining two distinct developments in one prize would require a clear statement of their shared physical significance."
        ]
      }
